  "abilities": [],
  "behavior": "It keeps nearly all of the normal juvenile's behavior: close-range combos, tail attacks, and the ability to burrow and ambush its target from below.",
  "interactionWithPlayer": "It is tougher than a regular juvenile but still much more manageable than an adult. Its main danger appears when its burrowing and venom attacks combine with pressure from other enemies during a wave.",
  "interactionWithCreatures": "It often appears in O.R.C. encounters alongside other creatures. This lets it take advantage of distractions created by other enemies to approach, burrow, or attack while the player focuses on another threat.",
  "strategy": "Use Busting damage and try to kill it before the O.R.C. adult when both appear together, since it requires far less damage to bring down. Interrupt its burrowing attempts whenever possible and, if the event allows turrets, use them: it takes roughly triple damage from turret fire.",
